  "root_cause": {
    "hypothesis": "The grid-stride loop bound `i <= N` causes an out-of-bounds read of a[N]/b[N] and write to c[N], one element past the allocated buffers of size N*sizeof(float).",
    "mechanism": "Buffers da/db/dc are allocated with N*sizeof(float) bytes, so valid indices are 0..N-1. The kernel loops `for (int i = tid; i <= N; i += stride)`, so at least one thread executes with i==N and performs `c[N] = a[N] + b[N]`. Depending on whether the memory page just past the allocation is mapped and readable, this either returns garbage (producing FAIL_NUMERIC where c[0] is overwritten by a stride-winner thread whose i==N wraps into observed elements, or shows nonzero max_abs_err at boundary) or triggers hipErrorIllegalAddress on the next hipDeviceSynchronize().",
    "confidence": 0.99,
    "bug_type": "out_of_bounds",
    "affected_lines": [
      33,
      34
    ]
  },
  "patch_plan": {
    "summary": "Change the grid-stride loop bound from `i <= N` to `i < N`.",
    "diff": "@@ __global__ void vector_add ...\n-    for (int i = tid; i <= N; i += stride) {\n+    for (int i = tid; i < N; i += stride) {\n         c[i] = a[i] + b[i];\n     }",
    "risks": [
      "None \u2014 the fix restricts iteration to valid indices only; all N elements are still computed because tid ranges cover [0,N)."
    ],
    "expected_effect": "STATUS: PASS with MAX_ABS_ERR < 1e-4 and no hipErrorIllegalAddress.",
    "validation_steps": [
      "recompile with `hipcc -O2 -std=c++17`",
      "rerun the binary",
      "check STATUS: PASS and MAX_ABS_ERR near 0"
    ]
  },
